MID_EV12_055_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_055_m01_001: Hello and welcome to another Anna administrative\nannouncement for the Heroic Games!
MID_EV12_055_m01_002: Your last battle was astounding. The main matches\nexceed all expectations!
MID_EV12_055_m01_003: And there are more on the horizon. Including your\nsecond!
MID_EV12_055_m01_004: Have you already uncovered who your opponent is?
MID_EV12_055_m01_005: <TLP>Match: Second Main Match of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Fiery Mane\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV12_055_m01_006: <NCA>Remark on the opponent.
MID_EV12_055_m01_007: <NCB>Remark on Anna.
MID_EV12_055_m01_008: <ACA>The White-Maned Demon. I have longed to face him.
MID_EV12_055_m01_009: <ACA>He is renowned as the strongest in the arena, is he\nnot? And he is a criminal who betrayed his people.
MID_EV12_055_m01_010: <ACB>You are primed for a fight. Yet you hold back.
MID_EV12_055_m01_011: <ACB>Me? You must be joking! I'm an administrator,\nnot a warrior! Eheh... Heh...
MID_EV12_055_m01_012: I guess I should have asked earlier, but... Why is the\narena so different for the main matches?
MID_EV12_055_m01_013: I mean, we were fighting on ships, recreating history!\nNow...not so much.
MID_EV12_055_m01_014: Why'd they change it? This is the real deal!
MID_EV12_055_m01_015: There's no need for elaborate staging when the\ncaliber of the combatants is so high.
MID_EV12_055_m01_016: And, between you and me, the creator of those set\npieces is actually fighting in the main matches.
MID_EV12_055_m01_017: She really needs to focus on that, so production\nkind of...fell to the side.
MID_EV12_055_m01_018: Weird that a behind-the-scenes person would climb\non stage! I wonder why.
MID_EV12_055_m01_019: Honestly, she's pretty famous. You may have heard\nof her. Dante?
MID_EV12_055_m01_020: Dante, the master auteur? Are you kidding?
MID_EV12_055_m01_021: Wait... Dante? Our Dante? She was behind all\nof that?
MID_EV12_055_m01_022: I read her book, The Rise of the White-Maned\nDemon. I couldn't put it down!
MID_EV12_055_m01_023: Dagdan literature? A page-turner? You have\nmy attention.
MID_EV12_055_m01_024: Have you read it, Esmeralda? It's really good!
MID_EV12_055_m01_025: Books? Me? I don't...do...books.
MID_EV12_055_m01_026: Oh, you'll like this one. I'll buy you a copy.
MID_EV12_055_m01_027: It's really popular! Since...oh, last year. And you can\nlend it to Fabio after you finish it!
MID_EV12_055_m01_028: Then we can all sit up late talking about it! I'll\nmake the coffee.
MID_EV12_055_m01_029: Uh, thank you. I'll give it a go.
MID_EV12_055_m01_030: I'm not convinced this is the book for me, but...\nSweetie, what do you think? Should I?
MID_EV12_055_m01_031: When you are through reading, Fabio, I am next\nin line.
MID_EV12_055_m01_032: Most certainly. I see that you would enjoy it.
MID_EV12_055_m01_033: Yes, thanks to Elfrida. She chooses books for us\nto read.
MID_EV12_056_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_056_m01_001: It is dangerous to let Dietrich do as he likes. Much\ntoo dangerous.
MID_EV12_056_m01_002: I agree. He has toddled too far from the nursery.
MID_EV12_056_m01_003: If he doesn't behave—if he stands against us when it\nmatters most—it will mean trouble.
MID_EV12_056_m01_004: We should think about defeating him now, before\nit's too late. We have the means.
MID_EV12_056_m01_005: We and the Guardians of the Compass together\nwould make short work of him.
MID_EV12_056_m01_006: No. I will not permit it.
MID_EV12_056_m01_007: Why hesitate? Are you having doubts?
MID_EV12_056_m01_008: That man has a grip on you.
MID_EV12_056_m01_009: In your heart of hearts, have you betrayed Father?
MID_EV12_056_m01_010: You accuse me, but what of you? You've been\nmaking quite a spectacle of yourself lately.
MID_EV12_056_m01_011: I hear stories about you. People see you visiting the\ndungeons. And your private matches...
MID_EV12_056_m01_012: Why complain? I'm getting the job done.
MID_EV12_056_m01_013: I have the freedom to do what I want, so I use it. It's\nthe one perk of playing Solel's mistress.
MID_EV12_056_m01_014: I will consider how best to handle Dietrich. There is\nno cause for concern.
MID_EV12_056_m01_015: Do not take matters into your own hands.
MID_EV12_056_m01_016: Ah, well. Look at the time. I must go.
MID_EV12_056_m01_017: You seem unsettled of late. What are you up to?
MID_EV12_056_m01_018: I have no obligation to tell. My life is my life.
MID_EV12_056_m01_019: If she's going, then I'm going. Just one piece of\nadvice first...don't forget your objective.
MID_EV12_056_m01_020: And before you ask, no, I'm not leaving to have my\nfun. I'm going to take care of that little favor for you.
MID_EV12_056_m01_021: Once it's over with, we can check the cauldron. So\noff I go.
MID_EV12_056_m01_022: I will leave it in your hands.
MID_EV12_056_m01_023: Oh, Dietrich...
MID_EV12_057_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_057_m01_003: I see the talk of his beauty wasn't exaggeration.\nUnderstatement, if anything.
MID_EV12_057_m01_046: 
MID_EV12_057_m01_047: 
MID_EV12_057_m01_048: 
MID_EV12_057_m01_049: 
MID_EV12_057_m01_004: But you can't let the fine make of a blade distract you\nfrom its sharpness. He's dangerous.
MID_EV12_057_m01_005: Heh heh HEH! Let's see how handsome you are\nwhen I've cut off your ears and that pretty little nose!
MID_EV12_057_m01_006: You are flashy, but that is all. It is a show.
MID_EV12_057_m01_007: I see the fear in your eyes. And more than anything,\nit is me you fear.
MID_EV12_057_m01_008: Wh-what? I ain't afraid of you. I'm just quiverin' to\ncarve you up!
MID_EV12_057_m01_009: Now that I get a good look at you, you aren't\nhalf bad!
MID_EV12_057_m01_010: Can't compare to Sweetie, of course. This whole\nclown act, though...
MID_EV12_057_m01_011: You're really overdoing it. It's not working.
MID_EV12_057_m01_012: We have spent much time in proximity to Dietrich.\nWe know what is real and what is a mere pose.
MID_EV12_057_m01_036: Heh heh HEH! Let's see how handsome you are\nwhen I've cut off your ears and that pretty little nose!
MID_EV12_057_m01_037: You are flashy, but that is all. It is a show.
MID_EV12_057_m01_038: I see the fear in your eyes. And more than anything,\nit is me you fear.
MID_EV12_057_m01_039: Wh-what? I ain't afraid of you. I'm just quiverin' to\ncarve you up!
MID_EV12_057_m01_040: Now that I get a good look at you, you aren't\nhalf bad!
MID_EV12_057_m01_041: Can't compare to Sweetie, of course. This whole\nclown act, though...
MID_EV12_057_m01_042: You're really overdoing it. It's not working.
MID_EV12_057_m01_043: We have spent much time in proximity to Dietrich.\nWe know what is real and what is a mere pose.
MID_EV12_057_m01_001: Now that I see him up close—the White-Maned\nDemon is handsome, isn't he?
MID_EV12_057_m01_002: Handsome? Not compared to Sweetie!
MID_EV12_057_m01_034: Now that I see him up close—the White-Maned\nDemon is handsome, isn't he?
MID_EV12_057_m01_035: Handsome? Not compared to Sweetie!
MID_EV12_057_m01_013: I have burned to duel you, White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV12_057_m01_014: Let us waste no more time. I will split your breast.
MID_EV12_057_m01_015: You speak with such murderous coldness. Tell me—\nwhat is it you fight for?
MID_EV12_057_m01_016: Why, for the fight itself. The pleasure that comes\nonly when we stake our lives.
MID_EV12_057_m01_017: If I do not fight, the thirst builds... And only blood\nwill slake it.
MID_EV12_057_m01_018: Caution, Bertrand. I don't think he's going to make\nthis easy for us.
MID_EV12_057_m01_019: Unbelievable as it may seem, this is the man who\ntook out the Sea Tyrant.
MID_EV12_057_m01_044: Cetus?! I thought such an act was not humanly\npossible.
MID_EV12_057_m01_045: Was it because of that sword? Ah, mustn't get\ndistracted—battle at hand. I'll write this down later.
MID_EV12_057_m01_022: How many have fallen to your hand, Dietrich?
MID_EV12_057_m01_023: I ended the first when I was a boy of but nine.
MID_EV12_057_m01_024: After I felled a hundred, I ceased my count.
MID_EV12_057_m01_025: Dietrich, what is it that you wish for? If you triumph\nin these games, what will you seek?
MID_EV12_057_m01_026: I apologize, but I cannot say. I will tell the Divine\nSovereign in time.
MID_EV12_057_m01_027: Fine. Judging by all I've learned about you, I'm sure\nit will be nothing pleasant.
MID_EV12_057_m01_028: Whatever your wish, I'm about to deprive you of it.\nDo not think ill of me.
MID_EV12_057_m01_029: Huh?
MID_EV12_057_m01_030: I have not heard this sound before. Answerer, are\nyou afraid?
MID_EV12_057_m01_031: Is it his axe you fear...or is it him?
MID_EV12_057_m01_032: Be not afraid. I am always at your side.
MID_EV12_057_m01_033: We stand together, my comrade.
MID_EV12_058_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_058_m01_001: You are known as Raksha...are you not?
MID_EV12_058_m01_002: My name is Lyrah. And my true name is\nthe Beckoner.
MID_EV12_058_m01_003: I am a Nabatean. For us, revealing our true name is\nsignificant. Did you know?
MID_EV12_058_m01_004: Tell me what it is you want.
MID_EV12_058_m01_005: If I were to tell you this land will be destroyed, would\nyou believe me?
MID_EV12_058_m01_006: <NCA>Accept it.
MID_EV12_058_m01_007: <NCB>Inquire.
MID_EV12_058_m01_008: <ACA>If so, it is no concern of mine.
MID_EV12_058_m01_009: <ACA>Most people would not just accept that. I never\nunderstand what you're thinking.
MID_EV12_058_m01_010: <ACB>An astounding notion. Tell me more.
MID_EV12_058_m01_011: My father, Balor, will soon be revived. And when he\nis, the underworld will engulf everything.
MID_EV12_058_m01_012: Join me. Please, you must. So we can be together.
MID_EV12_058_m01_013: I wish to be with you up until the moment of\nyour death.
MID_EV12_058_m01_014: These feelings... I... I have never felt them before.
MID_EV12_058_m01_015: Please, tell me we'll be together. I—
MID_EV12_058_m01_016: I will go mad otherwise!
MID_EV12_058_m01_017: Your father... He is strong.
MID_EV12_058_m01_018: Of course. Stronger than Mars, stronger than\nDagda—stronger than anyone.
MID_EV12_058_m01_019: However confident you are in your own strength,\nknow that you have no chance against him.
MID_EV12_058_m01_020: And that is why you will find me standing against\nyou both. For that fight is what I truly desire.
MID_EV12_058_m01_021: What?
MID_EV12_058_m01_022: Since I was born, I have strode through hell.
MID_EV12_058_m01_023: Let the world be consumed by its shadow. For me it\nchanges nothing.
MID_EV12_058_m01_024: Battle against the strong is the one thing that brings\nme fulfillment.
MID_EV12_058_m01_025: The pleasure I find at the ragged edge between life\nand death is the only thing that sates me.
MID_EV12_058_m01_026: It may be that my ancestral curse is not solely\nto blame.
MID_EV12_058_m01_027: If there is such a thing as a creator, then I was\ncreated with grave flaws.
MID_EV12_058_m01_028: Foolishness!
MID_EV12_058_m01_029: I do not think we walk the same path.
MID_EV12_058_m01_030: Ngh...
MID_EV12_058_m01_031: She is very beautiful, isn't she? You suit each other.
MID_EV12_058_m01_032: I guess I have to ask... Do you love her?
MID_EV12_058_m01_033: <NCA>Affirm.
MID_EV12_058_m01_034: <NCB>Remain silent.
MID_EV12_058_m01_035: <ACA>I suppose I might.
MID_EV12_058_m01_036: <ACA>If that's true, then why did you chase her off?
MID_EV12_058_m01_037: <ACB>Hmm.
MID_EV12_058_m01_038: <ACB>We could be together. But merely being together is\nnot love.
MID_EV12_058_m01_039: To strip life to its essence, to strive, to clash, to fray...\nTo push with all might to see who is strongest...
MID_EV12_058_m01_040: If there is to be love, I would have it be in this form.
MID_EV12_058_m01_041: Do you not agree? I could accept death if it was at\nher hands.
MID_EV12_058_m01_042: Are you kidding? Do I agree?
MID_EV12_058_m01_043: Maybe I could let you go. Maybe I'd even let her\nhave you.
MID_EV12_058_m01_044: But I've thought about it, and you know what? No!\nNot now!
MID_EV12_058_m01_045: Uh... *sigh*
MID_EV12_059_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_059_m01_001: Dietrich...
MID_EV12_059_m01_002: You have chosen your own path over me. Wretched.
MID_EV12_059_m01_003: It doesn't matter what road you take. Everyone\narrives at the same destination.
MID_EV12_059_m01_004: We will meet again in Father's underworld.
MID_EV12_059_m01_005: There's no need to put on a brave face.
MID_EV12_059_m01_006: Do not worry. I have excised all my feelings for\nthis man.
MID_EV12_059_m01_007: Are we moving forward? Finally!
MID_EV12_059_m01_008: Indeed. It is time to advance our plan to its\nnext phase.
MID_EV12_059_m01_009: We will move on the day of the Empire's founding—\nthe day of the Dagdan Declaration. 
MID_EV12_059_m01_010: Oh, yes... My heart's racing.
MID_EV12_059_m01_011: I will use the time till then to take care of some\nloose ends that need tying up.
MID_EV12_059_m01_012: Good. You have a critical part in this.
MID_EV12_059_m01_013: If you can deal with problems before they arise, all\nthe better.
MID_EV12_059_m01_014: Eishet, you must keep Solel's eyes off of us.\nDistract him.
MID_EV12_059_m01_015: That's my cue. Guess I'll go give him a show.
MID_EV12_059_m01_016: Ohh... I can't wait to see his face when he figures out\nwhat's happening.
MID_EV12_059_m01_017: I want to see Father again.
MID_EV12_059_m01_018: When that happens, Babbu, we'll have to say\ngoodbye. That'll be sad.
MID_EV12_059_m01_019: At least it seems Lyrah has finally overcome her\ndesire for Dietrich.
MID_EV12_059_m01_020: Everything culminates in her role. She can't afford\nany distractions.
MID_EV12_059_m01_021: Does she look forward to it? Birthing not just Father\ninto the world, but the underworld too?
MID_EV12_059_m01_022: I've waited so long. I can't stand to wait anymore!